***SOS!!*** **Hillside needs help!** The trees for our tree planting event on May 16th showed up waaaay too early and we need to get them planted before they die! We are moving the planting event up to this weekend, both days, starting at 9am until ??. If you can help at all, we would appreciate it! See the events posted on Trailbot for more details;

* [https://trailbot.com/trails/morc/news/hillside-tree-planting-saturday](https://trailbot.com/trails/morc/news/hillside-tree-planting-saturday)&#x20;
* [https://trailbot.com/trails/morc/news/hillside-tree-planting-sunday](https://trailbot.com/trails/morc/news/hillside-tree-planting-sunday)&#x20;

Feel free to reach out to Derek with questions! [HillsideMTBPark@gmail.com](mailto:HillsideMTBPark@gmail.com)

Hey Friends!&#x20;

We are super excited to start using Trailbot for volunteer tracking with MORC trails. **We need some help with this transition.**

MORC is looking for a volunteer to help us coordinate the transition to **Trailbot for Volunteers.** You'd be putting together training materials, video directions, and helping trail stewards use Trailbot to help coordinate, manage and track volunteers. we think this would be a great opportunity for some high school students who need volunteer hours (for racing, NHS, school, or because they are great people), or someone who's good at putting systems together. Hoping to get a couple events off the ground this spring, and then transition most of our trails to using the system to announce trail work events.&#x20;

Click on Volunteering for any trail, explain that you'd like to help as a volunteer coordinator. We'll take it from there!

The MORC Board

eventItems.content:
**This is typically the last trail work session of the season, late September can be TBD too so keep an eye here for changes.**

Lebanon Hills has trail work sessions nearly every Tuesday through summer. Details on specific tasks for the evening will be added a day or two prior to the work session. Come out and spend the evening throwing dirt, moving rocks, or rolling logs while talkin' about your dream bike.

No experience needed, nor anything to bring, we provide the tools and direction on tasks for the evening. We just recommend wearing something that can get dirty (pants and sturdy shoes/boots suggested) and other personal protective items like gloves and glasses. Waivers need to be signed and safety speech before trail work begins is required.&#x20;
